1
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:48,000
The movie that leaves all other sequels behind!

2
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Bugs Bunny's 3rd Movie: 1001 Rabbit Tales is a animation,
comedy, family film directed by Chuck Jones.

3
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:12,000
If Bugs Bunny were to direct his signature inquiry--"What's
up, doc?"--toward the modern-day Warner Bros.

4
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:54,000
creative team, he wouldn't be far off.

5
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:36,000
For 1001 Rabbit Tales, they've doctored up a batch of classic cartoons featuring the carrot muncher and
his bumbling comrades and bundled them, near seamlessly, into a feature-length film.

6
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Here's the premise: Bugs and Daffy, both book salesmen, are
competing to sell the most copies of a kids' book.

7
00:25:54,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Instead of burrowing a beeline to his sales territory (he should have made a left at
Albuquerque), Bugs ends up in the castle of Yosemite Sam, here a harem-leading honcho.

8
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Sam's pain-in-the-spurs son, Prince Abalaba, needs somebody to read him stories; Bugs, who'd sooner
take the job than suffer the alternative, that involving being boiled in oil, signs on.

9
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Bugs Bunny / Daffy Duck / Porky Pig / Yosemite Sam / Sylvester / Sylvester, Jr. / Speedy Gonzales / Tweety / Genie
/ Hassan / Big Bad Wolf / Beanstalk Giant / Elvis Gorilla / Stork (voice), played by Mel Blanc.

10
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Witch Hazel (voice), played by Bea Benaderet.

11
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:48,000
Elmer Fudd (voice), played by Arthur Q. Bryan.

12
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Granny / Mother Gorilla / Goldimouse (voice), played by June Foray.

13
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:12,000
Old Storyteller (voice), played by Shepard Menken.

14
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:54,000
Prince Abba-Dabba (voice), played by Lennie Weinrib.

15
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
Bugs Bunny's 3rd Movie: 1001 Rabbit Tales (also known as Bugs Bunny's 1001 Rabbit Tales) is a
1982 American animated fantasy comedy film produced and directed by Friz Freleng.

16
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:18,000
It combines classic Warner Bros.

17
01:02:54,000 --> 01:03:00,000
cartoon shorts with new animation, with Bugs Bunny serving as the story host.

18
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:42,000
The film explores themes of cartoon, compilation, package film.

19
01:10:18,000 --> 01:10:24,000
The tone is lighthearted.
